WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV v3.0 — eco-avalanche (180s) Narrator Cecily

1
00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:07.607
First, across life and computing, intelligence climbs a nine-step ladder through one repeating signal ratchet.

2
00:00:08.167 --> 00:00:11.269
Second, today's AI stalls at step five,

3
00:00:11.269 --> 00:00:16.201
tool use, because routine jobs wake giant models from scratch.

4
00:00:16.761 --> 00:00:21.454
Third, compiling verified answers into low-energy lookup reflexes

5
00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:24.992
crosses that wall and unlocks the top four steps.

6
00:00:25.552 --> 00:00:32.730
Today's frontier AI systems can draft code, call external software tools, and search databases, yet every routine

7
00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:39.907
request still wakes billions of numerical weights from scratch. Pouring more megawatts into data centers buys raw

8
00:00:39.907 --> 00:00:48.038
capability at steep electrical cost, leaving the software industry bottlenecked at step five of a nine-step intelligence ladder.

9
00:00:48.598 --> 00:00:54.460
Think back to your very first afternoon balancing a bicycle down a quiet street. At first your

10
00:00:54.460 --> 00:01:01.820
conscious cortex burned intense focus correcting every tiny wobble, but once your nervous system verified what worked,

11
00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:08.618
it compiled balance downward into fast cerebellar and spinal reflexes so your mind could scan the road ahead.

12
00:01:09.178 --> 00:01:18.887
Comparing major evolutionary leaps—from bacterial quorum sensing and myelinated nerves to spoken human language—against seventy-six years

13
00:01:18.887 --> 00:01:26.329
of computer science reveals the exact same three-part ratchet at every jump. First, make signaling cheap;

14
00:01:26.329 --> 00:01:34.904
second, gate action behind a strict verification threshold; third, compile proven solutions into fast, low-energy memory.

15
00:01:35.464 --> 00:01:43.069
Below the compilation threshold, every repeated question pays the full electrical bill of cold-start neural generation.

16
00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:49.395
Once automated checks certify a solution and freeze it into a compact lookup table or deterministic

17
00:01:49.395 --> 00:01:56.936
routine, verified completions per joule surge upward across steps six, seven, eight, and nine without losing accuracy.

18
00:01:57.496 --> 00:02:05.190
Our three-dimensional ratchet view shows noisy candidate proposals entering on the left, clearing strict emerald verification

19
00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:12.023
rings at the center, and crystallizing into quiet event-driven wakeups at step six, single-cycle Boolean lookup

20
00:02:12.023 --> 00:02:19.225
circuits at step seven, tamper-evident provenance at step eight, and energy-scheduled operating systems at step nine.

21
00:02:19.785 --> 00:02:28.113
In controlled experiments uniting ten classic AI paradigms—spanning symbolic search, Bayesian inference, evolutionary routines, and

22
00:02:28.113 --> 00:02:34.979
neural world models—no single method passed half our hundred-task suite alone, yet compiled synthesis passed

23
00:02:34.979 --> 00:02:43.244
ninety-eight tasks while inline circuit-board current sensors measured nine-to-twenty-seven-fold gains in verified work per joule.

24
00:02:43.804 --> 00:02:52.442
Scientific honesty demands separating today's lab measurements from tomorrow's predictions across eighteen dated milestones spanning

25
00:02:52.442 --> 00:02:58.920
one month to ten years, each paired with a concrete falsifier test. And wherever long-horizon steps

26
00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:06.314
touch human neural links, strict opt-in consent, local power limits, and instant user revocation remain absolute.
